Write a function using *args to sum any number of values;
The * before (1, 2, 3) spreads the tuple into separate arguments — so Python sees it as Sum(1, 2, 3), not Sum((1,2,3))
def Sum(*args):
    add=0
    for i in args:
         add+=i
    return add
print(Sum(*(1,2,3)))
#you can add print(Sum(1, 2, 3))
print(Sum((1, 2, 3)))

